-- title:
--   Gauge bound for GL₃ Jacquet–Whittaker cell functions
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, with completion $\mathbb Q_v$ = `v.adicCompletion ℚ`, let $\chi = (\chi_0,\chi_1,\chi_2)$ be a triple of multiplicative homomorphisms $\mathbb Q_v^{\times}\to\mathbb C^{\times}$, each locally constant, and assume that the product character $\chi_0\chi_1\chi_2$ takes values of complex absolute value $1$ on every unit $u\in\mathbb Q_v^{\times}$. Let $\Phi:\mathbb Q_v^{3}\to\mathbb C$ be locally constant with compact support, and let $B$ be a real number. The assertion is that there exist $t\in\mathbb N$ and $C\in\mathbb R$ such that, for every $g\in\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$ subject to the two constraints $$\frac{|\det g|\cdot L(g)}{M(g)^{2}}\le B,\qquad \frac{M(g)}{L(g)^{2}}\le B,$$ one has $$\bigl\|\,\mathrm{jacquetWhittaker3}\ v\ \chi\ \Phi\ g\,\bigr\|\ \le\ C\Big/\Big(\frac{|\det g|\,L(g)}{M(g)^{2}}\cdot\frac{M(g)}{L(g)^{2}}\Big)^{t}.$$ Here `detSize` $g=|\det g|$, `lastRowSup` $L(g)$ is the maximum of the norms of the three entries $g_{2,0},g_{2,1},g_{2,2}$ of the bottom row, and `minorSup` $M(g)$ is the maximum of the norms of the three $2\times 2$ minors $g_{1,j}g_{2,j'}-g_{1,j'}g_{2,j}$ formed from the lower two rows, for $(j,j')=(0,1),(0,2),(1,2)$; the two displayed quantities are the simple-root sizes of $g$. The function being estimated is the value at $g$ of `jacquetWhittaker3`, namely the stabilised truncated Jacquet integral `jacquetValue` of the right translate by $g$ of the cell section `cellSectionOf` $v\,\chi\,\Phi$, which is the function supported on the big cell `bigCell3` whose value there is `cellValue` $v\,\chi$ times $\Phi$ evaluated at `cellRatio`.
--
--   This is the local gauge (polynomial growth) estimate for the Whittaker function attached to a principal-series cell section of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$: on each cone cut out by bounding the two simple-root sizes by $B$, the Whittaker function is bounded by a fixed negative power of the product of those root sizes. It feeds the construction of the local Whittaker functionals and their Laurent expansions in the cubic-induction step of the Langlands–Tunnell argument, and is used in the analysis of the cyclic subspace generated by coefficient functions of the principal series.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_exists_norm_jacquetWhittaker3_le_of_rootSize_le.lean

